            "heading": "The Cancer Medicine They Tried to Hide.",
            "body": "<p>In the early 1900s, John D. Rockefeller, also known as the \"Father of Western Medicine\", saw a way to make billions from medicine.</p><p>But there was one problem.</p><p>Natural remedies like soursop leaves had been used to treat illness for hundreds of years, and they were his biggest competition.</p><p>Rockefeller used his oil money to replace natural medicine with drugs made from petroleum.&nbsp;</p><p>He paid schools to teach doctors about drugs instead of natural treatments.</p><p>Doctors who refused to follow the new rules lost their licenses, and some were even sent to jail.</p><p>He then helped fund the American Cancer Society to control what people knew about cancer and hide natural remedies like soursop.</p><p><strong>Natural medicine wasn't forgotten.</strong></p><p><strong>It was pushed aside for profit.</strong></p>",
            "background": "#f2f7ef",
            "accent": "#4f7847"
          }
        },
        "story_continuation": {
          "type": "story_continuation",
          "settings": {
            "show_section": true,
            "position": "after_trust",
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/1201E8CB-A8BB-449C-8717-E3F0A3B6C76D.png",
            "eyebrow": "",
            "heading": "Why Was Soursop Erased From Cancer Medicine?",
            "body": "<p>For hundreds of years, families across the Caribbean used <strong>soursop leaves to treat illness.</strong> Generation after generation, cancer never touched their families.</p><p>But everything changed when cancer treatment became a billion-dollar business.</p><p><strong>Soursop was a threat.</strong></p><p>Why? Because a simple leaf could cost the drug industry billions if people chose it over expensive treatments.</p><p>So powerful drug companies buried research, silenced natural healers, and tried to erase soursop from medicine.</p><p><strong>They tried to bury the truth. But they couldn’t bury soursop’s story.</strong></p>",
            "background": "#fbfcf7",
            "accent": "#4f7847"
          }
        },
